   "source": [
    "# Baseline Model Evaluation Report: Earthquake Magnitude Prediction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e57c86cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Objective\n",
    "To establish baseline performance for predicting earthquake magnitude (Mag) using only spatial and depth features (Latitude, Longitude, Depth) from the provided dataset. Three baseline models were evaluated: mean predictor, median predictor, and linear regression."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b161c8fa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Baseline Models Chosen\n",
    "**Mean Predictor:**\n",
    "Always predicts the mean magnitude from the training set. This serves as a naive baseline.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Median Predictor:**\n",
    "Always predicts the median magnitude from the training set. Robust to outliers.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Linear Regression:**\n",
    "Attempts to find a linear relationship between Latitude, Longitude, Depth and Magnitude."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a98dd7df",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Performance Evaluation\n",
    "Models were evaluated using standard regression metrics:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Mean Absolute Error (MAE)**: Average absolute difference between predictions and actual values.\n",
    "- **Root Mean Square Error (RMSE)**: Square root of average squared difference.\n",
    "- **R² Score (Linear Regression only)**: Proportion of variance in target explained by the model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "960c1204",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary Table of Results\n",
    "| Model             | MAE   | RMSE  | R²     |\n",
    "|------------------|-------|-------|--------|\n",
    "| Mean Predictor    | 0.347 | 0.459 | -      |\n",
    "| Median Predictor  | 0.329 | 0.482 | -      |\n",
    "| Linear Regression | 0.347 | 0.459 | 0.001  |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eca3a6df",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Analysis and Insights\n",
    "**Baseline Model Performance:**\n",
    "Mean and median predictors performed similarly, as expected. Linear regression showed minimal improvement.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Initial Hypotheses vs. Results:**\n",
    "Expected spatial and depth features might offer predictive signal. Results show they are weak predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Model Robustness:**\n",
    "Used median imputation and feature scaling. 80/20 train/test split provided fair evaluation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6a0300de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What We Learned and Next Steps\n",
    "**Key Takeaways:**\n",
    "- Naive predictors set a solid benchmark.\n",
    "- Linear regression does not outperform significantly.\n",
    "- Low R² indicates need for richer features.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next Steps:**\n",
    "- Add features like fault type, seismic moment, historical activity.\n",
    "- Explore advanced models like decision trees or neural nets.\n",
    "- Apply domain knowledge for feature engineering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "714515d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Conclusion\n",
    "These baseline results provide a starting point for future modeling. They demonstrate the importance of meaningful features and guide us to enrich the dataset and model complexity in subsequent steps."
   ]
  }
